[{:seon.task/name "a-send-parks-like-a-receive"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the blocking-calls audit of 2026-10-25 (docs/failure-points.md; items 5, 6, 28). What exists: seon.sock/recv! parks on a main carrier (MSG_DONTWAIT, then poller/wait-ready, sock.clj:195-203) but the sends do not: write-all! (sock.clj:230-238) calls lib/c-write on a blocking socket and c-sendmsg (sock.clj:25, :304, fd passing) is :blocking, so every message to root from the agent, the test child and the fork server (fork_server.clj run-loop send!) holds the carrier, and with it every other fiber, while root is slow to drain a full socket buffer. Correct, at the one edge: send with MSG_DONTWAIT on a fiber of a main carrier, on EAGAIN park on poller/wait-ready fd :write and retry the rest; a short send continues from the offset; sendmsg the same. Linux needs MSG_NOSIGNAL (no SO_NOSIGPIPE). Wiki owed in docs/flow.md in the same commit: in a process that runs only on the main carrier a foreign call that waits on another process or the network must park (nonblocking fd plus wait-ready) or be bounded by its own work; :blocking only makes the call collect-safe. Proof to write: a sender to a peer that does not read keeps its process answering its other fibers until the peer drains."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
